===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|India|transitive}} To [[act]] as a [[#Noun|shroff]], [[especially]] {{lb|en|historical}} to [[inspect]] [[coin]]s to [[detect]] [[debasement]], [[counterfeit]]s, [[clip]]ping, etc. for a [[commission]].
#* '''1757''' July 7, {{w|Robert Clive}}, letter, cited in John Malcolm, ''Life of Robert, Lord Clive'', Vol. I, page 278:
#*: I represented... that the money could not be divided till it was '''shroffed'''.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 14 1906|journal=Saturday Review|page=451
|passage=The potential revenues of China are immense, but they are ‘'''shroffed'''’... by every hand through which they pass.}}

